| Build — assemble, compile and link the HostFS module with the DDE.
| Produces <Obey$Dir>.HostFS,ffa: one module that runs from ROM as well as
| from the RMA.  Obey halts at the first failing command, so any error
| below is the one to read.  The o directory must exist already.
|
| The output is named HostFS, not HostFS,ffa: link -rmf types it Module
| itself, which a host share stores as HostFS,ffa.  Named HostFS,ffa on
| HostFS 2.x, the linker creates it as Data -- HostFS,ffd on the host --
| and then cannot open the HostFS,ffa it asked for.
|
| No cmhg and no C:o.stubs.  cmhg's header imports __RelocCode, and the
| stubs patch their vectors in place: both write into the module image at
| initialisation, which from ROM is a data abort (see c.hostfs, s.head).
| o.relocs is decaof's list of relocations: it must hold only PC-relative
| ones, since an absolute address would be wrong wherever the module lands.
Set HostFS$Dir <Obey$Dir>
Dir <Obey$Dir>
objasm -o o.head s.head
cc -c -zps1 -ffah -o o.hostfs c.hostfs
link -rmf -o HostFS o.head o.hostfs
decaof -r o.head o.hostfs { > o.relocs }
Echo Built <HostFS$Dir>.HostFS
